<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/glossary#galleon">Glossary</a> · Term</p><h1 class="enc-title">Galleon</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">A galleon was a large, multi-decked sailing ship used from the sixteenth century for war and long-distance trade. The galleon was the workhorse of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spanish-empire">Spanish Empire</a>, carrying <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/silver">silver</a> across the Atlantic and Pacific in convoy fleets, and it formed the core of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spanish-armada">Spanish Armada</a> of 1588.</p></div>
